A number of cases in China initially had chest oppression and palpitations.
In some, the disease progressed to pneumonia, multi-organic insufficiency and death.
It's called an incubation period.
COVID-19 incubation period is usually from five to six days, but it can vary from two to fourteen days.
Ninety-seven per cent of people who have symptoms do so within 11.5 days of the infection. Not all of those infected reportedly have any symptoms.
The role of these asymptomatic bearers is not yet fully known; however, preliminary evidence suggests they can contribute to the spread of the disease.
The proportion of those infected who do not have symptoms is currently unscathed and is being studied. The Korea Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (KCDC) reported that 20 per cent of confirmed cases remained asymptomatic during hospitalization.
The Chinese National Health Commission began including asymptomatic cases in daily cases on April 1. Of the 166 infections on that day, 130 (78 per cent) were asymptomatic when the test was carried out.
